# Atlas — contractor invoicing: submit, two-step approval, pay via PayGrid (Sprint 09)
# Login first (see auth.http) and paste the bearer token below.
# The happy path here runs as an org admin, who is permitted at every step.

@host = http://localhost:5000
@token = PASTE_TOKEN_HERE

### Register a contractor (HR/admin) → 201
POST {{host}}/api/v1/contractors
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Dana Devlin",
  "email": "dana@example.com",
  "country": "USA",
  "payoutCurrency": "USD"
}

### List this org's contractors
GET {{host}}/api/v1/contractors
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Submit an invoice for the contractor (HR/admin, on their behalf) → 201, status "Submitted"
# Paste the contractor id from the create response above. Every line must be in the
# contractor's payout currency (USD here) — a EUR line would be a 422.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/invoices
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "contractorId": "PASTE_CONTRACTOR_ID",
  "lines": [
    { "description": "Design work", "amount": 100.00, "currency": "USD" },
    { "description": "Build work", "amount": 50.00, "currency": "USD" }
  ]
}

### Mixed-currency invoice → 422 (single-currency invariant)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/invoices
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "contractorId": "PASTE_CONTRACTOR_ID",
  "lines": [
    { "description": "USD line", "amount": 100.00, "currency": "USD" },
    { "description": "EUR line", "amount": 50.00, "currency": "EUR" }
  ]
}

### Step 1 of 2 — HR approves (Submitted → HrApproved)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/invoices/PASTE_INVOICE_ID/hr-approve
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Admin-approve BEFORE hr-approve → 422 (the two-step order is structural)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/invoices/PASTE_SUBMITTED_INVOICE_ID/admin-approve
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Step 2 of 2 — admin authorises the money (HrApproved → Approved)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/invoices/PASTE_INVOICE_ID/admin-approve
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Pay (Approved → Paid) — money moves through the PayGrid ACL → 200, status "Paid"
POST {{host}}/api/v1/invoices/PASTE_INVOICE_ID/pay
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Pay before both approvals → 422 (only an Approved/Failed invoice is payable)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/invoices/PASTE_UNAPPROVED_INVOICE_ID/pay
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### The invoice with its lines, total, status, and vendor reference
GET {{host}}/api/v1/invoices/PASTE_INVOICE_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List invoices (org-scoped, cursor pagination as everywhere)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/invoices?limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### The reconciliation query — every Paid invoice (finance checks these against the vendor statement)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/invoices?status=Paid
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Reconcile one invoice against the provider's settlement (async settlement, no webhooks until S10)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/invoices/PASTE_INVOICE_ID/reconciliation
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
